# Configuration for v-github-mirror
# Format: USER|REPO_URL|BRANCH|DESTINATION_PATH_RELATIVE_TO_HOME|RETENTION_MODE|RETENTION_COUNT
#
# Recommended destination layout: git/<repo-name>
#   -> Stored at /home/<user>/git/<repo-name> (0700 <user>:<user>, outside all web roots,
#      and automatically included in HestiaCP backups as 'User Directory: git').
#   -> Domain-scoped web/<domain>/private/<folder> paths are also supported.

# Example 1: Mirror a repo into the user's dedicated git/ folder (Recommended Overwrite)
admin|https://github.com/your-org/repo.git|main|git/repo|overwrite

# Example 2: Mirror a private repo with Versioned snapshots (keep last 5 copies)
client1|git@github.com:my-org/website-source.git|production|git/website-source|versioned|5

# Example 3: Mirror with Smart Retention (Daily/Weekly/Monthly snapshots in git/ or web/<domain>/private/)
# Requires enabling ENABLE_DAILY_BACKUPS etc. in /etc/hestiacp-github-mirror.settings
anotheruser|git@github.com:client-x/astro-project.git|master|git/astro-project|backup
